Upgrade phpmailer/phpmailer from 6.4.0 to 6.5.0

PHPMailer 6.4.0 can load untrusted code when the language-file path comes
from a caller (GHSA-77mr-wc79-m8j3, CVE-2021-3603) and can call an
attacker-supplied validator (CVE-2021-34551). We do not call either entry
point, but the pin is in our lockfile and shows up in every scan. 6.5.0
fixes both; composer update --no-install regenerated the lock.
